# x86 STD SURFACE — `std/arch_x86/` Call Graph and AST-Shim Wire Plan

File: openOODA/audit/x86-std-surface.oot
THIS FILE IS GENERATED — DO NOT EDIT. Source: ripgrep inventory of `ooda/std/arch_x86/`, `ooda/oodac/`, and `ooda/scripts/` on 2026-08-25. Fresh after RFC 0011 Turn 2.

Logline: This door names every public symbol that `std/arch_x86/` exposes, every external caller that reaches it, and the small set the new typed-AST shim (`ooda/oodac/x86_ast_typed.oo`) must wire in Turn 2 to retire the 25-arm token walker in `ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo:46-198`.

Setup: Reader has read `openOODA/FORMAT.oot`, `openOODA/rfcs/0011-x86-ast-pipeline.oot`, and `audit/x86-std-audit.oot`. The 95 files under `ooda/std/arch_x86/` form a complete x86-64 native toolchain (registers, ABI, encoder, syscalls, linker, codegen) that is currently not wired into the `oodac emit-x86` path; only seven `std_qa_*` scripts reach it.

Beats:
  1. Inventory 95 files into library versus fixture roles, with line counts and purpose.
  2. Map every external caller to the std fn it reaches (file:line).
  3. Pick the "must wire" set the AST shim needs to call to replace the token-walker arms.
  4. Name the fns whose prefix or signature will change in the new shim layer.
  5. List zero-call (dead) symbols that Turn 2 should leave alone or remove.
  6. Flag fns with too many responsibilities, hidden errors, or duplicated logic.

---

## 1. std/arch_x86/ file inventory

`ooda/std/arch_x86/` contains 95 `.oo` files (95 of 95, 0 missing), 3,326 lines total, 255 public fn or type declarations. Split: 15 library files (real codegen helpers) and 80 fixture files (single `verify_x86_<name>` entry point consumed by the `emit-x86` regression smokes).

