## 3. Must-wire set (AST shim, RFC 0011 Turn 2)

The new shim layer (replacing the 25-arm `x86_emit.oo:46-198` dispatch chain) must call the following `std/arch_x86/` fns to lower the typed AST into bytes. Each item cites the specific token-walker arm it replaces.

1. `elf64_link_executable` (`x86_linker.oo:121`) replaces the final fallback `x86_emit_linux64` (`x86_emit.oo:78, 198`) and the `x86_emit_elf.oo` shim. Use this for the per-program ELF writer.
2. `x86_encode_mov_rr` (`x86_encoder.oo:46`) replaces the SSA int-arith bodies behind `x86_emit_int_write` (`x86_emit.oo:121-124`) and the `+`/`-`/`*` arms of `x86_emit_alu.oo`.
3. `x86_encode_push` / `x86_encode_pop` (`x86_encoder.oo:28, 37`) replace `cg_emit_push_rbp` and the per-frame prologue in `x86_emit_alu.oo` and `x86_emit_loop.oo` for `x86_emit_while_loop` (`x86_emit.oo:151-154`).
4. `x86_encode_add_rr` / `x86_encode_sub_rr` / `x86_encode_xor_rr` (`x86_encoder.oo:54, 62, 70`) replace the inlined ALU in `x86_emit_int.oo`, `x86_emit_alu.oo`, and the constant-fold path `x86_fold_hello` (`x86_emit.oo:74-80`).
5. `x86_encode_mov_ri64` (`x86_encoder.oo:78`) replaces the constant-load bodies in `x86_emit_typed_let` (`x86_emit.oo:131-134`), `x86_emit_match_test` (`x86_emit.oo:146-149`), and `x86_emit_fib_test` (`x86_emit.oo:181-184`).
6. `sc_emit_sys_write` / `sc_emit_sys_exit` (`x86_syscalls.oo:134, 188`) replace the println path used by `x86_emit_greet_call` (`x86_emit.oo:116-119`) and the harvest fallback `x86_collect_prints` (`x86_emit.oo:197`).
7. `abi_arg_count` / `abi_arg_reg` / `abi_ret_reg` (`x86_abi.oo:26, 17, 30`) replace the per-arity SysV bodies in `x86_emit_id_call`, `x86_emit_snd_call`, `x86_emit_thd_call`, `x86_emit_fth_call`, `x86_emit_5th_call`, and `x86_emit_6th_call` (`x86_emit.oo:81-109`).
8. `abi_is_callee_saved` (`x86_abi.oo:38`) replaces the spilled-set in `x86_emit_rec.oo` (used by the recursion arm `x86_emit_free_test` at `x86_emit.oo:176-179`).
9. `abi_stack_aligned` (`x86_abi.oo:61`) replaces the per-fn frame-size math in `x86_emit_fn.oo` and `x86_emit_span.oo` (prologue for `x86_emit_multi_main` at `x86_emit.oo:136-139`).
10. `elf64_default_base` (`x86_linker.oo:109`) replaces the hardcoded 0x400000 in `x86_emit_elf.oo` for the per-file `.s` writer in `x86_emit_multi_main` (`x86_emit.oo:136-139`).
11. `x86_rax` / `x86_rdi` / `x86_rsi` / `x86_rdx` (`x86_regs.oo:13, 20, 19, 15`) replace the literal register codes 0/7/6/2 in `x86_emit_rsi.oo` and `x86_emit_rdx.oo` (the call-shape arms at `x86_emit.oo:86-99`).

(Acceptance: each item names an `oodac/x86_emit.oo` arm, so the AST shim has a precise replacement target for every line of the 25-arm chain.)

