## 4. Rename set (new shim naming)

Fns whose name or prefix will change in the new shim layer (or in any subsequent consolidation pass). The new shim favors `emit_<mnemonic>` and `x86_<noun>` over the current `cg_*`, `php_*`, `sc_*`, `avx2_*`, `elf64_*` prefixes.

1. `cg_emit_prologue` / `cg_emit_epilogue` / `cg_emit_push_rbp` / `cg_emit_pop_rbp` / `cg_emit_ret` / `cg_emit_mov_rsp_rbp` / `cg_emit_imm32_mov_rax` / `cg_emit_imm64_mov_rax` / `cg_emit_push_rdi` / `cg_emit_pop_rdi` (`x86_codegen.oo:118-178`) — drop `cg_` prefix; rename to `emit_*` so the shim does not carry a two-letter namespace that no other std module uses.
2. `sc_mov_rax_imm64` / `sc_mov_rdi_imm64` / `sc_mov_rsi_imm64` / `sc_mov_rdx_imm64` / `sc_mov_r10_imm64` / `sc_mov_r8_imm64` / `sc_mov_r9_imm64` / `sc_syscall_instr` / `sc_concat` / `sc_emit_sys_*` (`x86_syscalls.oo:18-188`) — drop `sc_` prefix; the `sc_` namespace is undefined anywhere else in `std/`.
3. `php_cmov_rr` / `php_cmove` / `php_cmovne` / `php_cmovl` / `php_cmovle` / `php_cmovg` / `php_cmovge` / `php_lea_*` / `php_mul_by_const` / `php_elim_redundant_mov` / `php_elim_dead_stores` / `php_pass` (`x86_peephole.oo:18-230`) — drop `php_`; rename to `emit_cmov_*` / `opt_lea_*` / `opt_pass` to expose the optimizer role.
4. `avx2_vex_prefix` / `avx2_emit_vmovdqa_*` / `avx2_emit_vpaddq_rr` / `avx2_emit_vpsubq_rr` / `avx2_emit_vpmullq_rr` / `avx2_emit_vpand_rr` / `avx2_emit_vpor_rr` / `avx2_emit_vpxor_rr` / `avx2_emit_vfmadd231ps_rr` / `avx2_auto_vec_int64_loop` (`x86_avx2.oo:36-126`) — rename to `simd_vpaddq_rr` etc; remove the `avx2_` umbrella so AVX-512 (residual) and SSE (residual) can land under one `simd_` namespace.
5. `elf64_emit_magic` / `elf64_emit_header` / `elf64_emit_pheader` / `elf64_emit_u16` / `elf64_emit_u32` / `elf64_emit_u64` / `elf64_concat` / `elf64_default_base` / `elf64_header_size` / `elf64_pheader_size` / `elf64_link_executable` / `elf64_link_with_layout` (`x86_linker.oo:15-148`) and `elf64_magic` / `elf64_build_executable` (`x86_elf.oo:13-39`) — two files duplicate the ELF64 header builder; collapse to one `x86_elf.oo` with `x86_elf_header` / `x86_elf_pheader` / `x86_elf_link` so the new shim has one import, not two.
6. `abi_arg_reg` / `abi_arg_count` / `abi_ret_reg` / `abi_ret_hi_reg` / `abi_is_callee_saved` / `abi_caller_saved_mask` / `abi_align_up` / `abi_stack_aligned` / `abi_red_zone_size` (`x86_abi.oo:17-65`) — rename to `x86_abi_arg_reg` etc; today these names collide with the identical-shape `aarch64_abi.oo` and a future `wasm_abi.oo` would collide too.
7. `x86_asm_new` / `x86_asm_emit_byte` / `x86_asm_emit_bytes` / `x86_asm_len` / `x86_asm_finish` (`x86_assembler.oo:18-53`) — keep names, but the `X86Assembler` struct's two-field record is parallel to a future `AArch64Assembler`; consider `x86_asm_*` prefix stays (it is unique today), but the struct type may want to move under a `core` namespace.

