## 5. Dead symbols (zero-call)

Fns or files with no external caller. Most are deliberate test inputs; a few are leftover that Turn 2 should consider deleting or wiring.

1. `verify_x86_direct_elf` (`x86_direct_elf.oo:11`) — single fn, no external caller, no fixture file. The file is 14 lines and exists only to be `import`ed by a smoke that does not exist.
2. `avx2_*` (all 14 fns in `x86_avx2.oo:17-128`) — zero external callers; imported only transitively by `std_qa_x86_selfhost.oo:12` which does not call any `avx2_` fn. The module is reachable only as a load-bearing import (the smoke fails if oodac cannot compile a file that mentions `avx2_vex_prefix`).
3. `php_*` (all 21 fns in `x86_peephole.oo:18-230`) — zero external callers; same transitive-import-only reachability as `avx2`. Optimizer is currently never invoked.
4. `cg_*` (all 26 fns and types in `x86_codegen.oo:20-178`) — zero external callers; the file is imported by nothing in `ooda/oodac/`, `ooda/scripts/`, or `ooda/runtime/`.
5. `matrix_compile_source` (`x86_matrix_compile.oo:53`) — has exactly one external caller (`std_qa_slice_matrix.oo:93`) and the only argument it accepts is the empty string, which it always returns `Err` on. Effectively a stub.
6. All 80 `verify_x86_*.oo` fixtures — zero direct callers in the `.oo` source. They are *consumed* by `oodac emit-x86` as the input to compile, not as functions to call. The `verify_x86_*` fn is a marker; the test runner is `scripts/x86_*_smoke.oo` which `process_exec`s the produced binary.
7. `elf64_link_with_layout` (`x86_linker.oo:136`) — zero callers; `elf64_link_executable` is the only externally used linker entry (`x86_native_cases.oo:119, 131, 143, 155, 167`; `x86_torture_cases.oo:195`).

